// Nursing: assessments, flowsheets, fluid balance, risk scores, devices, the
// medication administration record, tasks, handover, restraints, transfusion,
// education, assignment and downtime.
//
// Owning context : nursing  (Master Engineering Registry)
// Owning service : NursingService
// Trace          : SRS-NUR-001 … SRS-NUR-018
//
// Two rules shape this contract.
//
// Every bedside record carries two timestamps — when the observation was true
// of the patient, and when it reached the record — because SRS-NUR-003 requires
// a late entry to be identified as late and to carry the actual observation
// time. There is no single "timestamp" field anywhere in this file.
//
// A dose is identified by its order and its scheduled time, not by the
// submission that recorded it, because SRS-NUR-018 requires that re-keying a
// downtime paper chart twice cannot produce two administrations of the same
// dose.

